# Wave W17-X (Route 209): tower turf — pilgrim-path turf, drift flecks: a muted sage meadow carrying sparse cream and blush petal flecks, the flower drifts at the Forsaken Tower’s fence blown thin across the whole sward (design: flower drifts banked thick at its fence; bells for the remembered, rest for the travellers). Route 209’s own ground — split from Route 210’s deep ranch pasture beside it by the muteness and the petals (the pilgrim road remembers, the ranch road feeds) and from Route 201’s fresh shore green by register entire: this green has stood quiet beside a tower for a long time.
